Chapter: E1000ResetWedged
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Kernel chapter Pci

 The refusal half of the e1000 model, and the reason the model is in the
 catalog at all: a model that can only succeed is not a test of the
 driver that handles failure. Its `.vmargs` holds RST set forever, which
 is a part wedged in reset.

 Two things are asserted, and the second is the one with a history. The
 driver must report the device ABSENT rather than present, which it did
 not do until CL 12079: the fuel cap fired correctly after a million
 polls and the answer was discarded, so a part that never left reset came
 back as a healthy device with a valid address and a working ring pair.

 The second is that the refusal costs almost no heap. The reset is
 sequenced before the ring allocations precisely so a refused bring-up
 does not leak them, and on a bump allocator with no collector that leak
 would be permanent: about 66 KB per attempt, against the few dozen bytes
 the PciBar record costs. A band rather than an exact count, because the
 exact number moves with unrelated allocator work while the property
 being asserted does not.

Section: Fixtures

  found-dev : PciScanResult -> Maybe PciDevice
  found-dev (scan) = e1000-find scan

Section: Judges

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

 init-cost answers a pair the only way a chapter with no tuples can: the
 caller asks twice, and the device is brought up once per question. That
 is deliberate, because two bring-ups of a wedged part must both refuse.

  init-present : PciDevice -> Boolean
  init-present (dev) = (e1000-init dev).e-present

  init-cost : PciDevice -> Integer
  init-cost (dev) =
    let before = alloc-bytes 0
    in let d = e1000-init dev
    in let after = alloc-bytes 0
    in after - before

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let scan = pci-scan-bus 0
    in act
      when found-dev scan
        is Just (dev) -> act
          print-line-uni ("candidate found : yes")
          print-line-uni ("present         : " & yn (init-present dev))
          print-line-uni ("refusal under 1K: " & yn (init-cost dev < 1024))
        end
        is None -> print-line-uni ("candidate found : no")
    end
  end

